# Pre-commit: fast feedback on staged files

## Pattern

```
git commit
 └── hook runner (Husky, lefthook, pre-commit framework, …)
 └── lint-staged (or equivalent)
 └── per-package config
 └── shared policy: lint --fix → format (skip pure renames)
```

## Principles

- Run only on **staged** paths
- Stricter than CI global warn (e.g. `--max-warnings=0` on staged files)
- Same tool versions as CI (pin in lockfile / container)
- Fail fast — do not rely on CI as the first lint signal

